/Title (Overall, the results confirm the advantages and disadvantages associated with each approach. Traditional coding delivers complete control, unlimited customization, strong performance, robust security, and excellent scalability, at the cost of long development time, high cost, dependency on experienced developers, and difficult maintenance. Low-code delivers faster development, lower cost, an easier learning curve, visual development, and AI assistance, but comes with limited customization, platform dependency, and reduced suitability for extremely complex applications.)
